# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Activate Llanowar Elves for green mana and spend it to cast Grizzly Bears.
# Forcing: One Forest plus the Elf are the only two mana sources for the two-mana spell.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no battlefield or hand, so it makes no decisions.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the Elf produced mana and Grizzly Bears resolved.
#   LOSE = the spell was not cast before the one-turn deadline.
#   TIMEOUT = activation, payment, or resolution stopped advancing.
# Card roles:
#   Llanowar Elves — mana-ability lifecycle under test.
#   Grizzly Bears — observable consumer of the Elf's mana.
#   Forest — remaining mana source and human draw padding.
#   Mountain — opponent draw padding.
# Protocol path: mana action, ability creation, tap, mana payment, ability retirement, and creature resolution.

[metadata]
Name:Llanowar Elves Mana
Goal:Play the Specified Permanent
Targets:Grizzly Bears
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Tap Llanowar Elves for the mana needed to cast Grizzly Bears.

